# Close-out D9 (finding F36): the expiry and reconcile loops run only in the platform instance that holds the leader advisory lock, so two instances on one database never both run passes. The fault removes the election (Leader.Ensure always answers true): both instances then run the loops, the checker that counts the instances whose loops ran a pass reports two, and the test must say DOUBLE RUNNER.
GATE=loops-leader
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestLeader_ExactlyOneInstanceRunsThePasses (database integration test, real Postgres)
CMD=H_PG_ADMIN_DSN="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" bash tests/harness/run-db-tests.sh '^TestLeader_ExactlyOneInstanceRunsThePasses$'
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestLeader_ExactlyOneInstanceRunsThePasses
MESSAGE=DOUBLE RUNNER
